      "description": "Recommendation 1: Allow 870-872 only after inpatient claim same claim review confirms a sepsis diagnosis present with Physician or LIP documentation; exempt sepsis screening and members under 18. Exempt: sepsis screening, members under 18. Peer: Buckeye Health Plan (WellCare) requires 870-872 on the same inpatient claim with a sepsis diagnosis present, and Carolina Complete Health applies same-claim review plus Physician or LIP documentation to 870-872 with exemptions for sepsis screening and members under 18..\n\nIA \u2014 Implement pre- or post-pay medical record review on the same inpatient claim for DRG codes 720, 853-855, and 870-872 and diagnosis codes A41.9, R65.20, and R65.21, with physician or licensed independent practitioner documentation required and review within 60 days. Buckeye Health Plan (WellCare), Carolina Complete Health, and Centene all target 720, 853-855, and/or 870-872 in inpatient DRG review, and Buckeye/Centene apply same-inpatient-claim review with a 60-day window.. Exempt: sepsis screening.\nIA \u2014 Apply pre-payment review and post-payment review to DRG claims containing R65.2, and on the same inpatient claim validate R65.2 before and after payment. Molina and Parkland Community Health Plan both review R65.2 on DRG claims pre- and post-payment, with Parkland applying the check on the same inpatient claim..",
